      "amount": "1/4 cup",
      "notes": "+ garnish, if desired"
    }
  ],
  "instructions": [
    "preheat oven to 400°f (200°c).",
    "trim asparagus and cut into 1-inch pieces.",
    "in a large skillet, sauté onion and garlic until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "add chorizo (if using), chicken broth, and cook until liquid is almost completely evaporated, about 3 minutes.",
    "in a separate bowl, whisk eggs and season with salt and pepper.",
    "in a greased 9x13-inch baking dish, arrange asparagus in an even layer.",
    "sprinkle all-purpose flour over asparagus, then top with onion-garlic mixture, followed by eggs, and finally gruyère cheese.",
    "dot top of bake with butter.",
    "bake for 20 minutes, then increase oven temperature to broil and cook for an additional 2-3 minutes, or until cheese is melted and bubbly.",
    "let cool for 5 minutes before serving, garnished with fresh parsley, if desired."
  ],
